step	1	-	Quick guide step 1
line	<col=000080>Take a rake and a seed dibber from the leprechaun if you haven't got one already.</col>
step	2	-	Quick guide step 2
line	<str>Take a rake and a seed dibber from the leprechaun if you haven't got one already.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Talk to <col=800000>Pirate Pete</col> on the dock north-east of the Ectofuntus, decline the money.</col>
step	3	-	Quick guide step 3
line	<str>Take a rake and a seed dibber from the leprechaun if you haven't got one already.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Pirate Pete on the dock north-east of the Ectofuntus, decline the money.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Finish talking to <col=800000>Captain Braindeath</col>. Make sure you have at least one inventory space available to get the Blindweed seed (don't cancel the dialogue after the cutscene).</col>
step	4	-	Quick guide step 4
line	<str>Take a rake and a seed dibber from the leprechaun if you haven't got one already.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Pirate Pete on the dock north-east of the Ectofuntus, decline the money.</str>
line	
line	<str>Finish talking to Captain Braindeath. Make sure you have at least one inventory space available to get the Blindweed seed (don't cancel the dialogue after the cutscene).</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>If you still do not have a rake and a seed dibber, go down the ladder in the north-west corner. Head south-east past the spiders, and search the <col=800000>cupboard</col> there for the tools. Go back upstairs.</col>
step	5	-	Quick guide step 5
line	<str>Take a rake and a seed dibber from the leprechaun if you haven't got one already.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Pirate Pete on the dock north-east of the Ectofuntus, decline the money.</str>
line	
line	<str>Finish talking to Captain Braindeath. Make sure you have at least one inventory space available to get the Blindweed seed (don't cancel the dialogue after the cutscene).</str>
line	
line	<str>If you still do not have a rake and a seed dibber, go down the ladder in the north-west corner. Head south-east past the spiders, and search the cupboard there for the tools. Go back upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Leave the building to the south, down the stairs.</col>
step	6	-	Quick guide step 6
line	<str>Take a rake and a seed dibber from the leprechaun if you haven't got one already.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Pirate Pete on the dock north-east of the Ectofuntus, decline the money.</str>
line	
line	<str>Finish talking to Captain Braindeath. Make sure you have at least one inventory space available to get the Blindweed seed (don't cancel the dialogue after the cutscene).</str>
line	
line	<str>If you still do not have a rake and a seed dibber, go down the ladder in the north-west corner. Head south-east past the spiders, and search the cupboard there for the tools. Go back upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the building to the south, down the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Go south past the zombies and plant the blindweed in the south-eastern-most patch.</col>
step	7	-	Quick guide step 7
line	<str>Take a rake and a seed dibber from the leprechaun if you haven't got one already.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Pirate Pete on the dock north-east of the Ectofuntus, decline the money.</str>
line	
line	<str>Finish talking to Captain Braindeath. Make sure you have at least one inventory space available to get the Blindweed seed (don't cancel the dialogue after the cutscene).</str>
line	
line	<str>If you still do not have a rake and a seed dibber, go down the ladder in the north-west corner. Head south-east past the spiders, and search the cupboard there for the tools. Go back upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the building to the south, down the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go south past the zombies and plant the blindweed in the south-eastern-most patch.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Wait about 5 minutes (or a few seconds) for it to grow. (Warning: Nearby Zombie swabs can attack low and mid-levelled players. You can simply log out while waiting.) You'll receive an in-game message when it finishes growing. Pick the plant.</col>
