line	<str>Go south past the zombies and plant the blindweed in the south-eastern-most patch.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wait about 5 minutes (or a few seconds) for it to grow. (Warning: Nearby Zombie swabs can attack low and mid-levelled players. You can simply log out while waiting.) You'll receive an in-game message when it finishes growing. Pick the plant.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Captain Braindeath.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb-up the ladder in the south-east corner of the big room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Put the blindweed in the hopper (next to the pressure barrel) in the north-west corner of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Captain Braindeath. You will automatically get a bucket in your inventory if you don't have one.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the building using the stairs to the south, head west to the bridge, and open the gate north of 50% Luke.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north to the water source on the map, and fill the bucket with stagnant water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the brewery and add the stagnant water to the hopper. (Ectophial and talking to Pirate Pete is faster than walking back.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Captain Braindeath.</str>
line	
line	<str>Fish 5 sluglings. Fishing spots can be found east, south-east, and west of the farming patch. (Note: do not untangle the Fishbowl and net, if you do then use one on the other to retangle.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Put the sluglings in the pressure barrel by the hopper.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Captain Braindeath.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Talk to Davey in the room to the west, with all the bunk beds. (Note: He will only bless the wrench if you have 47 or more Prayer points)</col>
